# Sigma is ς at the end of a word, σ elsewhere: a σ typed last reads as ς.
σ ς final

# Elided words end in an apostrophe (σ' αγαπώ, μ' αρέσει, τ' όνομα): kept in
# the dictionary (find-supplement.py).
final-apostrophe

# The letters of modern (monotonic) Greek: the list's polytonic words (καὶ,
# τῶν) are left out.
letters αβγδεζηθικλμνξοπρσςτυφχψωάέήίόύώϊϋΐΰ

# find-supplement.py: Common Voice has little Greek text (41k words), so a
# word form seen this many times in Common Voice and Tatoeba together is
# enough, as for fi.
one-source 3
